      the markets for the investors’ own products. For example, Intel has invested
      in over 1,100 companies for a total of $7.9 billion, with the goal of nurturing
      technologies that could stimulate demand for Intel’s chip business. Another
      possible corporate investment strategy is to support start-ups that may be valu-
